# Digital-twin chat env vars (client-exposed; the PUBLIC_ prefix is required by Astro).
#
# You normally DON'T need to touch these — Astro loads env files BY MODE, so
# there's nothing to switch between local and prod:
#
#   .env.development  → used by `just web-dev`   (astro dev)    — committed; local Worker + test Turnstile key
#   .env.production   → used by `just web-build` (astro build)  — committed; deployed Worker + real site key
#   .env.local / .env.*.local → personal overrides for any mode — gitignored
#
# All PUBLIC_ values are non-secret (exposed to the browser by design). Real
# secrets — the Turnstile SECRET key and the Gemini key — live as Worker secrets
# / in worker/.dev.vars, never in web/.
#
# This file documents the keys. To override a value locally without editing the
# committed mode files, copy it into web/.env.local (gitignored).
PUBLIC_TWIN_ENDPOINT=https://jin-ho-lee-cv-twin.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
